om Firebase. No other component polls Virtius. |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-452-| 3 | Exact pixel dimensions for bug width, row height, logo/headshot sizes | OPEN | Determine during implementation with visual testing |\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md:453:| 4 | Should the score flash queue show all queued scores sequentially, or skip to the latest? | RESOLVED | Sequential per-team — each team row has its own independent queue. Each flash plays its full 10 seconds. Multiple teams can flash simultaneously. |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-454-| 5 | Color scheme for rotation tag — should it match team colors or be neutral? | OPEN | |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-455-| 6 | Should alternates/exhibition gymnasts be filtered out of \"now competing\"? | RESOLVED | No — all athletes are shown. Their scores just don't count toward team total (handled by API's `team.final_score`). |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-456-| 7 | Should the lineup card support showing multiple teams simultaneously? | RESOLVED | No — intentionally single-team only. `showLineup` is a single string value. |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-457-| 8 | How to handle `final_score` string type from API? | RESOLVED | Compare as strings for diff detection. Convert to `parseFloat()` for display formatting. |\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-458-| 9 | How to identify athletes across polls for score diffing? | RESOLVED | Use `gymnast_id` from Virtius API as primary key (already used in `output.html:4490`). Fallback: composite `team.short_name\\|normalizeName(full_name)` for contexts where `gymnast_id` is absent. |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-459-| 10 | Should Firebase writes be full rewrites or incremental? | RESOLVED | Incremental deltas only via `firebase.update()`. Full API response is NOT written — only changed paths. Critical for Firebase free tier over 2-3 hour competition with 5s polling. |\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-460-| 11 | How should the overlay handle offline/reconnect? | RESOLVED | On reconnect: immediate full poll (bypass interval timer), diff against last known state, write reconnect event to `lastError`. Firebase listeners auto-reconnect via SDK. |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-461-| 12 | How should score corrections during an active flash be handled? | RESOLVED | Interrupt active flash immediately, replace with corrected score flash, reset 10-second timer. |\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md:462:| 13 | Can the producer dismiss score flashes? | RESOLVED | Yes — DISMISS button per team in producer panel writes timestamp to `scoreBug/dismissFlash/{teamKey}`. Overlay clears flash if dismiss timestamp > flash start time. |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-463-| 14 | How should rotation be determined in multi-team meets? | RESOLVED | Minimum completed events across ALL teams + 1. Rotation only advances when every team has finished their current event. |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-464-| 15 | OBS browser source dimensions? | RESOLVED | 1920x1080 full screen with transparent background. Bug renders on right side. |\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md:465:| 16 | How does the lineup card interact with score flashes? | RESOLVED | Both operate independently. Lineup card stays visible above the bug while score flashes animate in the team rows below. Lineup card scores update live simultaneously with flashes. |\n--\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-8-\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-9-## 1. Problem Statement\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-10-\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-11-During live gymnastics broadcasts, viewers have no persistent on-screen indicator of team scores, current competition state, or recent scoring activity. Producers must manually trigger individual graphics for each score update, and there is no automated way to surface real-time competition data from the Virtius API as a persistent broadcast element.\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-12-\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md:13:The system needs a persistent \"score bug\" — similar to the score tickers in professional sports broadcasts — that stays on screen throughout the competition, automatically updates via API polling, and surfaces key information: team totals, individual score flashes, rotation info, and who is currently competing.\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-14-\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-15----\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-16-\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-17-## 2. Goals\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Te