raphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-451-| 2 | Should the producer panel poll Virtius independently or share data with the overlay? | RESOLVED | Single poller — overlay polls Virtius, writes **incremental deltas** to `scoreBug/liveData/` in Firebase. Producer panel AND GraphicsControl Athlete Spotlight both read from Firebase. No other component polls Virtius. |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-452-| 3 | Exact pixel dimensions for bug width, row height, logo/headshot sizes | OPEN | Determine during implementation with visual testing |\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md:453:| 4 | Should the score flash queue show all queued scores sequentially, or skip to the latest? | RESOLVED | Sequential per-team — each team row has its own independent queue. Each flash plays its full 10 seconds. Multiple teams can flash simultaneously. |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-454-| 5 | Color scheme for rotation tag — should it match team colors or be neutral? | OPEN | |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-455-| 6 | Should alternates/exhibition gymnasts be filtered out of \"now competing\"? | RESOLVED | No — all athletes are shown. Their scores just don't count toward team total (handled by API's `team.final_score`). |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-456-| 7 | Should the lineup card support showing multiple teams simultaneously? | RESOLVED | No — intentionally single-team only. `showLineup` is a single string value. |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-457-| 8 | How to handle `final_score` string type from API? | RESOLVED | Compare as strings for diff detection. Convert to `parseFloat()` for display formatting. |\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-458-| 9 | How to identify athletes across polls for score diffing? | RESOLVED | Use `gymnast_id` from Virtius API as primary key (already used in `output.html:4490`). Fallback: composite `team.short_name\\|normalizeName(full_name)` for contexts where `gymnast_id` is absent. |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-459-| 10 | Should Firebase writes be full rewrites or incremental? | RESOLVED | Incremental deltas only via `firebase.update()`. Full API response is NOT written — only changed paths. Critical for Firebase free tier over 2-3 hour competition with 5s polling. |\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-460-| 11 | How should the overlay handle offline/reconnect? | RESOLVED | On reconnect: immediate full poll (bypass interval timer), diff against last known state, write reconnect event to `lastError`. Firebase listeners auto-reconnect via SDK. |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-461-| 12 | How should score corrections during an active flash be handled? | RESOLVED | Interrupt active flash immediately, replace with corrected score flash, reset 10-second timer. |\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md:462:| 13 | Can the producer dismiss score flashes? | RESOLVED | Yes — DISMISS button per team in producer panel writes timestamp to `scoreBug/dismissFlash/{teamKey}`. Overlay clears flash if dismiss timestamp > flash start time. |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-463-| 14 | How should rotation be determined in multi-team meets? | RESOLVED | Minimum completed events across ALL teams + 1. Rotation only advances when every team has finished their current event. |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-464-| 15 | OBS browser source dimensions? | RESOLVED | 1920x1080 full screen with transparent background. Bug renders on right side. |\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md:465:| 16 | How does the lineup card interact with score flashes? | RESOLVED | Both operate independently. Lineup card stays visible above the bug while score flashes animate in the team rows below. Lineup card scores update live simultaneously with flashes. |\n--\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-8-\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-9-## 1. Problem Statement\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-10-\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-11-During live gymnastics broadcasts, viewers have no persistent on-screen indicator of team scores, current competition state, or recent scoring activity. Producers must manually trigger individual graphics for each score update, and there is no automated way to surface real-time competition data from the Virtius API as a persistent broadcast element.\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-12-\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md:13:The system needs a persistent \"score bug\" — similar to the score tickers in professional sports broadcasts — that stays on screen throughout the competition, automatically updates via API polling, and surfaces key information: team totals, individual score flashes, rotation info, and who is currently competing.\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-14-\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-15----\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-16-\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-17-## 2. Goals\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-18-\n--\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-63-   - Stick indicator (green circle with S) — men's meets only\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-64-4. Flash holds for 10 seconds\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-65-5. Slot-machines back down to default (logo + total)\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-66-6. Team total animates/highlights to show it updated\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-67-\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md:68:**Each team row operates independently** — every row manages its own score flash queue. If Team 1 and Team 2 both post scores at the same time, both rows flash simultaneously. If Team 1 posts 3 scores in rapid succession, Team 1's row queues and plays all 3 flashes sequentially (10s each) while Team 2's row is unaffected. There is no cross-team queue; each team's flash state is completely independent.\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-69-\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-70----\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-71-\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-72-### Story 3: Now Competing Display\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-73-\n--\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-246-Default → Now Competing (A) → Score Flash (A) → Default → Now Competing (B) → ...\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-247-```\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-248-\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-249-Score flash always takes over immediately, regardless of current state. If a score correction arrives during an active flash, the current flash is **interrupted** and replaced with a new flash showing the corrected score (resets the 10-second timer). After 10 seconds, returns to default. System then detects next athlete and cycle continues.\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-250-\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md:251:**Producer flash dismiss:** The producer can manually dismiss any active score flash via a DISMISS button in the producer panel. This immediately ends the flash and returns the row to default state. This is useful if a score was posted in error or the producer wants to clear the display. Dismissing a flash does not prevent future flashes — the next queued flash (if any) will fire, or the next detected score will trigger normally.\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-252-\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-253-### 4.4 Animation Specifications\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-254-\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-255-| Animation | Type | Duration |\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-256-|-----------|------|----------|\n--\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-486-- **Stale data indicator** — shows time since data last changed and count of unchanged polls. Informational only — helps producer distinguish \"no new scores\" from \"API might be stuck\"\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-487-- **Polling is independent of bug visibility** — start polling to pre-warm data before enabling the bug, or stop polling to freeze current state\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-488-- **Poll frequency is adjustable** — default 5s, can increase if API is slow or reduce for faster updates\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-489-- In **auto mode**, SHOW buttons become HIDE buttons (to dismiss if wrong)\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-490-- In **manual mode**, SHOW buttons confirm display\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md:491:- **Active Flashes section** — shows currently flashing scores with DISMISS button per team. Dismissing clears the flash immediately. Section only visible when a flash is active.\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-492-- Lineup team dropdown lists all teams in the competition\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-493-- Score flashes always fire automatically regardless of mode (but only when polling is active)\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-494-\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-495-### 7.2 Lineup Card + Score Flash Interaction\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-496-\n--\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-549-- [ ] Score diff engine uses `gymnast_id` as primary key (fallback: composite team+normalized name)\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-550-- [ ] Detects new scores and triggers slot-machine score flash\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-551-- [ ] Score flash shows: name, score, apparatus, start value (headshots added in Phase E)\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-552-- [ ] Score flash holds for 10 seconds then returns to default\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-553-- [ ] Score corrections interrupt active flash immediately (replaces with corrected score, resets timer)\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md:554:- [ ] Per-team independent flash queues (each team row manages its own queue)\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-555-- [ ] Producer can dismiss active flash via Firebase `scoreBug/dismissFlash`\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-556-- [ ] Team total animates when it updates (including corrections)\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-557-- [ ] Rotation number tag displays at top (inferred from ALL teams' data, not just first team)\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-558-- [ ] Bug slides in/out from right edge\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md-559-- [ ] Firebase path `scoreBug/enabled` controls visibility\n--\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/logs/claude-output.jsonl-1-=== Iteration 1 (Sat Feb 21 11:31:51 CST 2026) ===\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/logs/claude-output.jsonl-2-Tasks: 9 complete, 2 in progress, 117 remaining\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/logs/claude-output.jsonl-3-[Omitted long context line]\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/logs/claude-output.jsonl-4-[Omitted long context line]\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/logs/claude-output.jsonl:5:[Omitted long matching line]\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/logs/claude-output.jsonl-6-[Omitted long context line]\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/logs/claude-output.jsonl-7-[Omitted long context line]\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/logs/claude-output.jsonl-8-[Omitted long context line]\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/logs/claude-output.jsonl-9-[Omitted long context line]\ndocs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/logs/claude-output.jsonl-10-{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_017L6z6AXMP6YpCiweZaUnJY\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"No matches found\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"4cf8931b-9202-4746-824e-3d8bce4fed78\",\"uuid\":\"062dd4b4-dd78-4093-bb12-728e2bbfefb3\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"mode\":\"content\",\"numFiles\":0,\"filenames\":[],\"content\":\"\",\"numLines\":0}}\n--\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/logs/claude-output.jsonl-16-[Omitted long context line]\n/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/doc