{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_0187Vgz7yWBLL341gH2NyVWA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The plan confirms that A8 is:\n> **A8**: Implement per-team independent score flash queue (10s hold, then return to default) - Each team row has its own queue. Multiple teams can flash simultaneously.\n\nLooking at the implementation in the code, **this is already fully implemented**:\n\n1. **Per-team queues**: `state.flashQueues[teamIndex]` - each team has its own array of queued flashes\n2. **10s hold**: `state.flashDuration = 10000` ms, used in `displayNextFlash()` with `setTimeout(() => advanceFlashQueue(teamIndex), state.flashDuration)`\n3. **Return to default**: `clearFlashDisplay()` is called when queue is empty\n4. **Multiple teams flash simultaneously**: Each team has independent state in both `flashQueues` and `activeFlashes`\n\nThis was implemented as part of Task A5 (Score diff engine). The Quick Task Index notes for A5 say: \"Added flash queue system: triggerScoreFlash(), interruptFlash(), isFlashActive(), displayNextFlash(), advanceFlashQueue(), renderFlash(), clearFlashDisplay(). Score changes now trigger queued flashes per-team with correction detection.\"\n\nI should mark A8 as COMPLETE (since A5 already implemented it) and move to the next NOT STARTED task which is **A9: Team total highlight**."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1404,"cache_read_input_tokens":53070,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1404},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bff765a0-5962-484c-8261-9a83719f6208","uuid":"bad9eecd-9908-43ea-aea9-88e80df24e3a"}
