e read from this Firebase\n   116→path — no other component polls Virtius directly.\n   117→The overlay also writes detected \"now competing\" athletes to `scoreBug/detected/` and a heartbeat\n   118→timestamp on every poll cycle.\n   119→Producer actions (SHOW/HIDE, toggle, lineup, dismiss flash) write to Firebase, which the overlay\n   120→picks up via listeners.\n   121→\n   122→**Note:** This is the first overlay to use Firebase. Existing overlays use URL parameters only.\n   123→The overlay must initialize the Firebase SDK and establish realtime listeners.\n   124→\n   125→### 1.2 Data Flow\n   126→\n   127→```\n   128→┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   129→│  VIRTIUS API                                                         │\n   130→│  GET /session/{sessionId}/json                                      │\n   131→│  Polled every 5-10 seconds (by overlay ONLY)                        │\n   132→└──────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n   133→                       │\n   134→                       ▼\n   135→┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   136→│  SCORE DIFF ENGINE (in team-bug.html)                                │\n   137→│  ├── Compare previous poll vs current poll (keyed by gymnast_id)     │\n   138→│  ├── Convert final_score strings to floats for comparison            │\n   139→│  ├── Detect new scores → trigger score flash (per-team queue)       │\n   140→│  ├── Detect score corrections → interrupt active flash, re-flash    │\n   141→│  ├── Detect \"now competing\" → next athlete without score            │\n   142→│  ├── Infer rotation (min completed events across ALL teams + 1)     │\n   143→│  ├── Write DELTAS to Firebase (scoreBug/liveData/) — not full data  │\n   144→│  ├── Write heartbeat + stale poll count to Firebase                  │\n   145→│  ├── Write detected state to Firebase (scoreBug/detected/)          │\n   146→│  ├── Read dismissFlash from Firebase → clear active flash           │\n   147→│  └── On API error: keep stale data, backoff, write to lastError     │\n   148→└──────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n   149→                       │\n   150→              ┌────────┴────────┐\n   151→              ▼                 ▼\n   152→┌──────────────────────────┐  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   153→│  FIREBASE                 │  │  RENDERERS (in overlay)                    │\n   154→│  scoreBug/liveData/       │  │  ├── Team Row Renderer (logo + total)     │\n   155→│  scoreBug/detected/       │  │  ├── Score Flash Renderer (+ headshot)    │\n   156→│  scoreBug/lastError       │  │  ├── Now Competing Renderer (+ headshot)  │\n   157→│  (read by producer panel  │  │  ├── Rotation Tag Renderer                │\n   158→│   and GraphicsControl)    │  │  └── Lineup Card Renderer                  │\n   159→└──────────────────────────┘  └────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8eb195d-b364-428e-aa6c-e8fa0f12e95a","uuid":"046ed8b9-4852-4977-81f0-fc1076a374c4","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Team-Scores-Bug/PLAN-Team-Scores-Bug-2026-01-31.md","content":"| D6 | SHOW/HIDE now-competing | NOT STARTED | `show-controller/src/components/ScoreBugPanel.jsx` | — |\n| D7 | Lineup card controls | NOT STARTED | `show-controller/src/components/ScoreBugPanel.jsx` | — |\n| D8 | Write showLineup | NOT STARTED | `show-controller/src/components/ScoreBugPanel.jsx` | — |\n| D9 | Write nowCompeting | NOT