-├── Headshot resolver                    ├── dismissFlash ←────────  ├── DISMISS flash buttons\n105-├── Lineup card renderer                 ├── nowCompeting            ├── Reads detected/ & liveData/\n106-├── Writes detected state to FB ──→      ├── detected/ ──────────→  ├── SHOW/HIDE buttons\n107-├── Reads dismissFlash from FB ←───      ├── liveData/ ──────────→  └── Lineup card controls\n108-└── Firebase listener ←─────────────     ├── lastError\n--\n117-The overlay also writes detected \"now competing\" athletes to `scoreBug/detected/` and a heartbeat\n118-timestamp on every poll cycle.\n119:Producer actions (SHOW/HIDE, toggle, lineup, dismiss flash) write to Firebase, which the overlay\n120-picks up via listeners.\n121-\n122-**Note:** This is the first overlay to use Firebase. Existing overlays use URL parameters only.\n123-The overlay must initialize the Firebase SDK and establish realtime listeners.\n124-\n--\n265-| Task | Description | Status | Notes |\n266-|------|-------------|--------|-------|\n267:| A1 | Create `overlays/team-bug.html` boilerplate with transparent background, Firebase SDK init | COMPLETE | First overlay to use Firebase — must include SDK initialization. 1920x1080 full-screen source. Created with: Inter font, 1920x1080 viewport, transparent background, Firebase SDK v9.22 compat, URL param parsing for compId, basic state management, Firebase listeners for enabled/polling/automationMode/showLineup/dismissFlash. |\n268-| A1b | Initialize Firebase `scoreBug/` schema with default values on first load | COMPLETE | Uses Firebase transaction to safely initialize schema. If no data exists, writes full default schema. If data exists, merges defaults for missing fields only. Deep merges nested objects (config, liveData). Initialization runs before Firebase listeners are attached. |\n269-| A2 | Implement URL parameter parsing (`compId`) and read competition config from Firebase | COMPLETE | Implemented loadCompetitionConfig() which reads from Firebase `competitions/{compId}/config`. Loads virtiusSessionId, gender, and team names/logos (up to 6 teams). Also implemented renderTeamRows() to display teams with initial \"--\" totals. Sets rotation.total based on gender (6 for men, 4 for women). |\n270-| A3 | Implement Virtius API polling gated by Firebase `scoreBug/polling` flag | COMPLETE | Implemented poll() function: fetches from `https://api.virti.us/session/{sessionId}/json`, converts final_score strings to floats, stores API data in state for score diff engine, writes heartbeat on every poll. Poll interval listener restarts polling when interval changes. |\n271-| A3b | Write **incremental deltas** to Firebase `scoreBug/liveData/` after each poll | NOT STARTED | Use `firebase.update()` for only changed paths — NOT full rewrite. Critical for Firebase free tier. Also write heartbeat timestamp on every poll. Track stalePollCount and lastDataChangeTimestamp. |\n272-| A3c | Implement API error handling: stale data display, exponential backoff, write to `scoreBug/lastError` | NOT STARTED | On failure: keep last good data, double interval (max 30s), reset on success |\n--\n302-| Task | Description | Status | Notes |\n303-|------|-------------|--------|-------|\n304:| C1 | Build lineup card HTML/CSS layout (team header, numbered list, event total) | NOT STARTED | |\n305:| C2 | Populate lineup card from Virtius API data (athletes, scores, order) | NOT STARTED | |\n306:| C3 | Implement lineup card slide-up/down animation above bug | NOT STARTED | |\n307:| C4 | Connect Firebase listener for `scoreBug/showLineup` | NOT STARTED | |\n308:| C5 | Live-update lineup card scores as API polls return new data | NOT STARTED | |\n309-\n310-### Phase D: Producer Panel (P0)\n311-\n312-| Task | Description | Status | Notes |\n313-|------|-------------|--------|-------|\n--\n325-| D5c | Build active flash display with DISMISS button per team | NOT STARTED | Writes dismiss timestamp to `scoreBug/dismissFlash/{teamKey}`. Only visible when flash is active. |\n326-| D6 | Implement SHOW/HIDE buttons for now-competing per team | NOT STARTED | |\n327:| D7 | Build lineup card controls (team dropdown + show/hide) | NOT STARTED | |\n328:| D8 | Write Firebase `scoreBug/showLineup` on lineup toggle | NOT STARTED | |\n329-| D9 | Write Firebase `scoreBug/nowCompeting` on manual confirm | NOT STARTED | |\n330-| D10 | Migrate GraphicsControl.jsx Athlete Spotlight to read from `scoreBug/liveData/` | NOT STARTED | Remove independent Virtius polling from GraphicsControl (lines 216-269). Read from Firebase instead. |\n331-\n332-### Phase E: Headshot Integration (P1)\n333-\n--\n400-├── polling: false                  // boolean — API polling active (independent of enabled)\n401-├── automationMode: \"auto\"          // \"auto\" | \"manual\"\n402:├── showLineup: null                // null | teamKey string (intentionally single-team only)\n403-├── dismissFlash: {}                // { teamKey: timestamp } — producer dismisses active flash\n404-├── nowCompeting: {}                // { teamKey: athleteName | null } — producer overrides\n405-├── detected: {}                    // { teamKey: { athlete, gymnastId, apparatus } } — written by overlay\n406-├── heartbeat: null                 // timestamp — written by overlay on every poll cycle\n407-├── liveData: {                     // Written INCREMENTALLY (deltas only, not full rewrite)\n--\n454-| 5 | Color scheme for rotation tag — should it match team colors or be neutral? | OPEN | |\n455-| 6 | Should alternates/exhibition gymnasts be filtered out of \"now competing\"? | RESOLVED | No — all athletes are shown. Their scores just don't count toward team total (handled by API's `team.final_score`). |\n456:| 7 | Should the lineup card support showing multiple teams simultaneously? | RESOLVED | No — intentionally single-team only. `showLineup` is a single string value. |\n457-| 8 | How to handle `final_score` string type from API? | RESOLVED | Compare as strings for diff detection. Convert to `parseFloat()` for display formatting. |\n458-| 9 | How to identify athletes across polls for score diffing? | RESOLVED | Use `gymnast_id` from Virtius API as primary key (already used in `output.html:4490`). Fallback: composite `team.short_name\\|normalizeName(full_name)` for contexts where `gymnast_id` is absent. |\n459-| 10 | Should Firebase writes be full rewrites or incremental? | RESOLVED | Incremental deltas only via `firebase.update()`. Full API response is NOT written — only changed paths. Critical for Firebase free tier over 2-3 hour competition with 5s polling. |\n460-| 11 | How should the overlay handle offline/reconnect? | RESOLVED | On reconnect: immediate full poll (bypass interval timer), diff against last known state, write reconnect event to `lastError`. Firebase listeners auto-reconnect via SDK. |\n461-| 12 | How should score corrections during an active flash be handled? | RESOLVED | Interrupt active flash immediately, replace with corrected score flash, reset 10-second timer. |\n--\n463-| 14 | How should rotation be determined in multi-team meets? | RESOLVED | Minimum completed events across ALL teams + 1. Rotation only advances when every team has finished their current event. |\n464-| 15 | OBS browser source dimensions? | RESOLVED | 1920x1080 full screen with transparent background. Bug renders on right side. |\n465:| 16 | How does the lineup card interact with score flashes? | RESOLVED | Both operate independently. Lineup card stays visible above the bug while score flashes animate in the team rows below. Lineup card scores update live simultaneously with flashes. |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8eb195d-b364-428e-aa6c-e8fa0f12e95a","uuid":"4319bc75-c0cd-42dc-aff5-e6619532a670","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"44-| C2 | Lineup card populate | NOT STARTED | `overlays/team-bug.html` | — |\n45-| C3 | Lineup card animation | NOT STARTED | `overlays/team-bug.html` | — |\n46: