{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019xMqrR42K3HKoaR3CYua2v","type":"tool_result","content":"22-| **Automated Score Flashes** | Detect new scores via API polling and surface them with athlete info |\n23-| **Now Competing Detection** | Approximate who is currently on apparatus and display it |\n24:| **Producer Control** | Dedicated collapsible panel in producer view with on/off toggle, automation settings, lineup card triggers, and copy URL button |\n25-| **Scalable Team Support** | Work for dual meets (2 teams) up to 6-team competitions |\n26:| **Lineup Card Integration** | Toggleable lineup overlay that pops above the bug |\n27-\n28----\n29-\n30-## 3. User Stories\n31-\n32-### Story 1: Producer Enables Score Bug\n33-\n34-**As a** Producer running a dual meet broadcast\n35-**I want to** toggle the score bug on from the Score Bug panel in the producer view\n36-**So that** viewers see a persistent scoreboard on the right side of the screen\n--\n77-\n78-**Flow:**\n79:1. Score bug polls API and detects next athlete in lineup order without a score\n80-2. **Auto mode:** Bug automatically slot-machines to show \"now competing\" state:\n81-   - Athlete headshot\n82-   - Abbreviated name\n83-   - Apparatus short code\n84-3. **Manual mode:** Producer panel shows suggestion: \"K. Tokunaga (PH) likely up — [SHOW]\"\n85-   - Producer clicks SHOW to confirm\n86-4. When athlete's score arrives, \"now competing\" transitions directly to score flash (10 sec), then back to default\n87-\n88----\n89-\n90:### Story 4: Producer Toggles Lineup Card\n91-\n92-**As a** Producer\n93:**I want to** pop up a team's current event lineup above the score bug\n94:**So that** viewers can see the full lineup with scores\n95-\n96-**Flow:**\n97-1. In Score Bug panel, select team from dropdown\n98:2. Click \"Show Lineup\"\n99:3. Lineup card slides up from above the score bug:\n100-   - Team name + logo header\n101-   - Numbered athlete list with scores (or \"--\" if not yet competed)\n102-   - Apparatus icon + event total at bottom\n103:4. Lineup updates live as scores come in from API\n104:5. Producer clicks \"Hide Lineup\" to dismiss\n105-\n106----\n107-\n108-### Story 5: Score Bug in Multi-Team Meets\n109-\n110-**As a** Producer running a tri-meet or quad-meet\n111-**I want** the score bug to display all competing teams\n112-**So that** viewers can track all team scores\n113-\n114-**Flow:**\n115-1. Bug renders one row per team (3 rows for tri, 4 for quad, up to 6)\n116-2. All rows function independently (score flashes, now competing)\n117:3. Lineup card can be triggered for any team\n118-4. Layout scales vertically — each row is compact (logo + total on left, slot on right)\n119-\n120----\n121-\n122-### Story 6: Producer Controls Automation\n123-\n124-**As a** Producer\n125-**I want** control over whether \"now competing\" displays automatically or manually\n126-**So that** I can prevent incorrect athlete detection from going to air\n127-\n--\n149-├── Writes API data to Firebase ──→    ├── enabled                  never polls Virtius)\n150-├── Renders team rows from FB data     ├── automationMode\n151:├── Manages slot animations            ├── showLineup\n152-├── Resolves headshots (Firebase)      ├── liveData/ ──────────→   Reads live scores\n153-├── Writes detected state to FB ──→    ├── detected/ ──────────→   Displays suggestions\n154-└── Transparent background (OBS)       └── nowCompeting             SHOW/HIDE buttons\n155-```\n156-\n157-[Omitted long context line]\n158-\n159-**Heartbeat mechanism:** The overlay writes a `scoreBug/heartbeat` timestamp to Firebase on every successful poll cycle. The producer panel monitors this timestamp and displays a prominent \"Last poll: Xs ago\" indicator. If the heartbeat goes stale (>30 seconds old), the producer panel shows a warning: \"Overlay not polling — check OBS browser source.\" This covers cases where the overlay tab is closed, backgrounded (browser throttling), or crashed.\n160-\n161-**Note:** This is the first overlay to use Firebase for real-time state. Existing overlays use URL parameters only. The overlay will need to initialize the Firebase SDK and establish realtime listeners in addition to polling the API.\n--\n210-- Holds until score arrives, then transitions to score flash\n211-\n212:**Lineup card (above bug, producer-triggered):**\n213-```\n214-┌──────────────────────────────────────┐\n215-│  Navy                           [N]  │\n216-├──────────────────────────────────────┤\n217-│  1. Kody Tokunaga       4.4  13.300  │\n218-│  2. Matthew Petros      4.5  11.850  │\n219-│  3. Daniel Gurevich     4.5  13.350  │\n220-│  4. Jonah Soltz                  --  │\n221-│  5. Brian Solomon                --  │\n222-├──────────────────────────────────────┤\n--\n260-| Slot machine (down) | Vertical slide, content drops back to default | 0.4s ease |\n261-| Total score update | Brief highlight pulse (color flash or scale) | 0.5s |\n262:| Lineup card enter | Slide up from bug top edge | 0.4s ease |\n263:| Lineup card exit | Slide down into bug | 0.4s ease |\n264-\n265----\n266-\n267-## 5. Data Sources\n268-\n269-### 5.1 Virtius API\n270-\n271-**Endpoint:** `GET https://api.virti.us/session/{sessionId}/json`\n272-**Polling interval:** 5-10 seconds\n273-\n--\n280-| `team.name` / `team.short_name` | Team identification |\n281-| `team.events[].event_name` | Determine which apparatus team is on |\n282:| `team.events[].event_score` | Event total for lineup card |\n283-| `team.events[].gymnasts[].gymnast_id` | Stable athlete identifier (primary key for score diff engine) |\n284-| `team.events[].gymnasts[].full_name` | Athlete display name |\n285-| `team.events[].gymnasts[].first_name` / `last_name` | For abbreviated display (e.g., \"K. Tokunaga\") |\n286-| `team.events[].gymnasts[].final_score` | Individual score (null = hasn't competed) |\n287:| `team.events[].gymnasts[].order` | Lineup position |\n288-| `team.events[].gymnasts[].scores[].start` | Start value (difficulty) |\n289-| `team.events[].gymnasts[].bonus` | Stick bonus — `bonus > 0` means stuck landing (men's only) |\n290-\n291-### 5.2 Firebase\n292-\n293-| Path | Purpose |\n294-|------|---------|\n295-| `competitions/{compId}/config` | Session ID, team names, comp type |\n296-| `competitions/{compId}/scoreBug/*` | Bug control state (enabled, mode, etc.) |\n297-| `teamsDatabase/headshots/{name}` | Athlete headshot URLs |\n--\n304-  1. Find the event where some gymnasts have scores and some don't\n305-     (this is the currently active event for this team)\n306:  2. Sort gymnasts by lineup order\n307-  3. First gymnast without a final_score = \"now competing\"\n308-  4. If all gymnasts have scores = event complete, no one currently up\n309-```\n310-\n311:This is an approximation — the API doesn't have a real-time \"on apparatus\" field. It works well when scores are entered sequentially in lineup order.\n312-\n313-**All athletes are shown in the bug**, including alternates and exhibition gymnasts. Their scores appear in score flashes like any other athlete. However, only counting scores contribute to the team total — the team total comes from `team.final_score` in the API, which already excludes non-counting scores.\n314-\n315-**Reuse existing detection logic:** GraphicsControl.jsx (lines 216-269) already has a working \"now competing\" detection implementation for the Athlete Spotlight feature. Extract and reuse this logic rather than writing it from scratch.\n316-\n317-### 5.4 Rotation Detection Logic\n318-\n319-The Virtius API does not provide a \"current rotation\" field. The overlay infers rotation from the API data using **all teams** (not just one):\n320-\n321-```\n--\n395-├── polling: boolean              // API polling active (independent of enabled)\n396-├── automationMode: \"auto\" | \"manual\"\n397:├── showLineup: null | \"navy-mens\"  // Which team's lineup to show (null = hidden)\n398:│                                    // Intentionally single-team: only one lineup card at a time\n399-├── dismissFlash: {               // Producer flash dismiss (written by producer, read by overlay)\n400-│     \"navy-mens\": 1706745610000, // Timestamp of dismiss — overlay clears flash if active\n401-│     \"springfield-mens\": null\n402-│   }\n403-├── nowCompeting: {               // Manual overrides for now competing\n404-│     \"navy-mens\": \"Kody Tokunaga\",\n405-│     \"springfield-mens\": null\n406-│   }\n407-├── detected: {                   // Written by overlay, read by producer panel\n408-│     \"navy-mens\": {\n--\n477-└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n478-\n479:Lineup Card:\n480-  Team: [Navy          ▾]\n481-  [SHOW LINEUP]  [HIDE LINEUP]\n482-```\n483-\n484-- **Copy URL button** — copies the OBS browser source URL for the score bug overlay (`https://commentarygraphic.com/overlays/team-bug.html?compId=xxx`) to clipboard, same pattern as existing graphics URL copy\n485-- **Heartbeat indicator** — shows time since last overlay poll. Green (<10s), yellow (10-30s), red (>30s or overlay not running). If red, displays \"Overlay not polling — check OBS browser source\"\n486-- **Stale data indicator** — shows time since data last changed and count of unchanged polls. Informational only — helps producer distinguish \"no new scores\" from \"API might be stuck\"\n487-- **Polling is independent of bug visibility** — start polling to pre-warm data before enabling the bug, or stop polling to freeze current state\n488-- **Poll frequency is adjustable** — default 5s, can increase if API is slow or reduce for faster updates\n489-- In **auto mode**, SHOW buttons become HIDE buttons (to dismiss if wrong)\n490-- In **manual mode**, SHOW buttons confirm display\n491-- **Active Flashes section** — shows currently flashing scores with DISMISS button per team. Dismissing clears the flash immediately. Section only visible when a flash is active.\n492:- Lineup team dropdown lists all teams in the competition\n493-- Score flashes always fire automatically regardless of mode (but only when polling is active)\n494-\n495:### 7.2 Lineup Card + Score Flash Interaction\n496-\n497:When a lineup card is visible and a score flash fires for any team:\n498:- The **team row still animates the score flash normally** (slot machine up, 10s hold, slot machine down). The lineup card remains visible above the bug and is unaffected.\n499:- The **lineup card updates live** — the athlete's score appears in the lineup card list as soon as the API data arrives, which happens at the same time as the flash. This provides useful reinforcement: the viewer sees the flash in the team row and the lineup card score fill in simultaneously.\n500:- If the lineup card is open for the same team that's flashing, both updates happen together. If it's open for a different team, only that team's row flashes while the lineup card stays static (no new data for that team).\n501-\n502-### 7.3 OBS Browser Source Configuration\n503-\n504-The score bug overlay is designed for a **1920x1080 full-screen OBS browser source** with transparent background. The bug renders on the right side of the viewport; the left side is fully transparent, allowing camera feeds and other sources to show through.\n505-\n506-| Property | Value |\n507-|----------|-------|\n508-| Source dimensions | 1920x1080 |\n509-| Background | Transparent (CSS: `background: transparent`) |\n510-| Bug position | Right-aligned within the 1920x1080 viewport |\n--\n527-| **A** | Core Score Bug | P0 | Overlay page, API polling, team rows with totals, score flashes |\n528-| **B** | Now Competing | P0 | Auto-detection, manual mode, producer panel suggestions |\n529:| **C** | Lineup Card | P1 | Toggleable lineup overlay above bug |\n530-| **D** | Producer Panel | P0 | Collapsible panel in producer view with all controls and copy URL button |\n531-| **E** | Headshot Integration | P1 | Resolve and display athlete headshots in flashes |\n532-| **F** | Stick Indicator | P2 | Green circle + S for men's meets |\n533-| **G** | Multi-Team Scaling | P1 | Test and refine layout for 3-6 team meets |\n534-| **H** | Quad-Box Variant | P3 | Alternate layout for quad camera view (future) |\n535-\n536----\n537-\n538-## 9. Success Criteria\n539-\n--\n570-\n571-### Phase C Complete When:\n572:- [ ] Lineup card renders above the bug\n573-- [ ] Shows numbered athlete list with scores or \"--\"\n574-- [ ] Shows event total at bottom\n575-- [ ] Updates live as scores come in\n576-- [ ] Producer can trigger per team from panel\n577-- [ ] Slides up/down with animation\n578-\n579-### Phase D Complete When:\n580-- [ ] Collapsible \"Score Bug\" panel exists in producer view right column\n581-- [ ] Copy URL button copies OBS browser source URL to clipboard\n582-- [ ] On/off toggle controls bug visibility via Firebase\n--\n587-- [ ] Now competing suggestions shown with SHOW/HIDE buttons (reads from Firebase, no API polling)\n588-- [ ] Active flash display with DISMISS button per team (writes to `scoreBug/dismissFlash`)\n589:- [ ] Lineup card team selector and show/hide controls\n590-- [ ] API error indicator shown when polling fails (reads `scoreBug/lastError` from Firebase)\n591-- [ ] GraphicsControl.jsx Athlete Spotlight polling removed/replaced (reads from `scoreBug/liveData/` instead)\n592-\n593-### Phase E Complete When:\n594-- [ ] Headshots resolve from `teamsDatabase/headshots/` using existing normalization\n595-- [ ] Headshots display in score flash and now competing states\n596-- [ ] Graceful fallback when headshot not found (show without headshot)\n597-\n598-### Phase F Complete When:\n599-- [ ] Stick indicator (green circle + S) displays for men's meets when `bonus > 0` in API data\n--\n616-| **Score Flash** | Temporary display (10s) of an individual athlete's score within a team row |\n617-| **Now Competing** | Display of the athlete currently (approximately) on apparatus |\n618:| **Lineup Card** | Expandable overlay showing full team lineup for current event |\n619-| **Start Value (SV)** | Difficulty score / D-score for a routine |\n620-| **Stick Indicator** | Visual indicator that an athlete \"stuck\" their landing (men's only) |\n621-| **Rotation Tag** | Header element showing current rotation number |\n622-\n623----\n624-\n625-## 11. Related Documents\n626-\n627-| Document | Purpose |\n628-|----------|---------|"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8eb195d-b364-428e-aa6c-e8fa0f12e95a","uuid":"975e9dcc-6550-44dc-8075-5f132dd9a35c","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"22-| **Automated Score Flashes** | Detect new scores via API polling and surface them with athlete info |\n23-| **Now Competing Detection** | Approximate who is currently on apparatus and display it |\n24:| **Producer Control** | Dedicated collapsible panel in producer view with on/off toggle, automation settings, lineup card triggers, and copy URL button |\n25-| **Scalable Team Support** | Work for dual meets (2 teams) up to 6-team competitions |\n26:| **Lineup Card Integration** | Toggleable lineup overlay that pops above the bug |\n27-\n28----\n29-\n30-## 3. User Stories\n31-\n32-### Story 1: Producer Enables Score Bug\n33-\n34-**As a** Producer running a dual meet broadcast\n35-**I want to** toggle the score bug on from the Score Bug panel in the producer view\n36-**So that** viewers see a persistent scoreboard on the right side of the screen\n--\n77-\n78-**Flow:**\n79:1. Score bug polls API and detects next athlete in lineup order without a score\n80-2. **Auto mode:** Bug automatically slot-machines to show \"now competing\" state:\n81-   - Athlete headshot\n82-   - Abbreviated name\n83-   - Apparatus short code\n84-3. **Manual mode:** Producer panel shows suggestion: \"K. Tokunaga (PH) likely up — [SHOW]\"\n85-   - Producer clicks SHOW to confirm\n86-4. When athlete's score arrives, \"now competing\" transitions directly to score flash (10 sec), then back to default\n87-\n88----\n8