{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_017gyTmDzg2MMn81CCnomuCE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good - the flash state lives only in client-side `state.flashQueues` and `state.activeFlashes`, not in Firebase. The overlay writes to Firebase only when a flash is dismissed by writing to `dismissFlash/{teamIndex}`.\n\nNow let me check if there's any state I can read from Firebase to know which teams have active flashes. Let me search for what the overlay writes to Firebase about flash status:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":635,"cache_read_input_tokens":35670,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":635},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af9e7b0b-717a-4523-8596-08397b416ec3","uuid":"2461ffb1-12a7-4887-9774-abe5205e5983"}
