{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01NABpNRmNzbF3LUQyJt9GZy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The overlay doesn't write flash status to Firebase. The dismiss button should simply work for all teams - the producer clicks \"dismiss\" for a team and it sets `dismissFlash/{teamIndex}` to true. The overlay will process it if there's an active flash, or ignore it if there isn't.\n\nLooking at the D5 now-competing display, each team has a teamIndex. I should add a dismiss button to each detected now-competing entry. But actually, the task says \"Dismiss flash button\" - this should be a way to dismiss the current score flash that's showing, not the now-competing display.\n\nLet me think about the UX:\n1. Flash shows a score update for a team\n2. Producer wants to dismiss it early (before the 10s hold)\n3. They click \"Dismiss\" for that team\n\nThe Now Competing Display shows which athletes are currently competing. The flash would show for any team that just got a score. I should add dismiss buttons that can clear any active flash.\n\nSince we don't have flash state synced to Firebase, the simplest approach is to show dismiss buttons for each team that exists in the competition. Let me check what team data is available:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":256,"cache_read_input_tokens":36305,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":256},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af9e7b0b-717a-4523-8596-08397b416ec3","uuid":"f4f70090-5658-4b68-8f6b-a2ce41457c9f"}
