{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AfqeMvsESvmq4vjgAqB89p","type":"tool_result","content":"   915→    /**\n   916→     * Render initial team rows based on competition config.\n   917→     * Called after loadCompetitionConfig() to show teams before API polling starts.\n   918→     */\n   919→    function renderTeamRows() {\n   920→      const container = document.getElementById('teamRows');\n   921→      if (!container) return;\n   922→\n   923→      container.innerHTML = state.teams.map((team, idx) => `\n   924→        <div class=\"team-row\" data-team-index=\"${team.index}\">\n   925→          <div class=\"team-fixed\">\n   926→            <img class=\"team-logo\" src=\"${team.logo}\" alt=\"${team.name}\" onerror=\"this.style.display='none'\">\n   927→            <div class=\"team-total\" id=\"teamTotal${team.index}\">${team.total}</div>\n   928→          </div>\n   929→          <div class=\"team-slot\" id=\"teamSlot${team.index}\">\n   930→            <div class=\"slot-content\" id=\"slotContent${team.index}\">\n   931→              <!-- Score flash / now competing content populated dynamically -->\n   932→            </div>\n   933→          </div>\n   934→        </div>\n   935→      `).join('');\n   936→\n   937→      console.log('Team rows rendered:', state.teams.length);\n   938→    }\n   939→\n   940→    /**\n   941→     * Update team total display element (A4).\n   942→     * Called when API polling detects a change in team.final_score.\n   943→     * Adds highlight animation on value change.\n   944→     * @param {number} teamIndex - 1-based team index\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b43ae3c4-0fd8-41a7-a6bd-fc65dff4dae1","uuid":"a37350b7-982d-4c5c-9026-42c3e5415222","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/overlays/team-bug.html","content":"    /**\n     * Render initial team rows based on competition config.\n     * Called after loadCompetitionConfig() to show teams before API polling starts.\n     */\n    function renderTeamRows() {\n      const container = document.getElementById('teamRows');\n      if (!container) return;\n\n      container.innerHTML = state.teams.map((team, idx) => `\n        <div class=\"team-row\" data-team-index=\"${team.index}\">\n          <div class=\"team-fixed\">\n            <img class=\"team-logo\" src=\"${team.logo}\" alt=\"${team.name}\" onerror=\"this.style.display='none'\">\n            <div class=\"team-total\" id=\"teamTotal${team.index}\">${team.total}</div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"team-slot\" id=\"teamSlot${team.index}\">\n            <div class=\"slot-content\" id=\"slotContent${team.index}\">\n              <!-- Score flash / now competing content populated dynamically -->\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      `).join('');\n\n      console.log('Team rows rendered:', state.teams.length);\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * Update team total display element (A4).\n     * Called when API polling detects a change in team.final_score.\n     * Adds highlight animation on value change.\n     * @param {number} teamIndex - 1-based team index","numLines":30,"startLine":915,"totalLines":2329}}}
